<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n15181" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄρκιος</span></b>  (A), <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">α</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			Arat.
			741
		</span></i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ος</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>
		<i><span class="en">
			<u>AP</u>
			11.59
		</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
			Maced.
		</span></i>): (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρκέω</span>):—
			Ep.
		
		Adj.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be relied on, sure, certain,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὔ οἱ ἔπειτα ἄρκιον ἐσσεῖται
			φυγέειν</span> he shall have no <i>hope</i> to escape, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				2.393
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νῦν ἄρκιον ἢ ἀπολέσθαι ἠὲ
				σαωθῆναι</span> one of these is <i>certain,</i> to perish
			or be saved, <i><span class="en">
				15.502
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μισθὸς δέ οἱ ἄ.
			ἔσται</span> a <i>sure</i> reward, <i><span class="en">
				10.304
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				18.358
			</span></i>, but, a <i>sufficient</i> reward in <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Op.</u>
				370
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βίος ἄ.</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				501
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				577
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>enough, sufficient,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄρκιον εὑρεῖν</span> to be sure of
			having enough, ib.<i><span class="en">
				351
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				2.799
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				8.13
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄφρα . . σφίσιν ἄρκιος
			εἴη</span> that he might be <i>sufficient</i> for them, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				25.190
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δέμας ἄρκιος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Opp.
					<u>C.</u>
					3.185
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>H.</u>
				3.601
			</span></i>; <i>helpful, useful,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παντὶ γὰρ ἄ. ἐστι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nic.
					<u>Th.</u>
					508
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Opp.
				<u>C.</u>
				3.173
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄρκια νούσων</span>
			<i>remedies against</i> . . , <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Th.</u>
				837
			</span></i>: c. inf., <i>able to</i> . . , <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				51a
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Cer.</u>
				35
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ίως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hsch.
				</span></i>
			
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> in comp. sense, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄρκιον ἦν θνᾴσκειν</span>”
				<i>it were better . . ,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					AP
					9.154
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Agath.
			</span></i>).</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
